## 7. API service (`server.ts`)

| Endpoint | Behaviour |
|---|---|
| `POST /jobs` | Body `{ F, C }`. Both must be integers with `1 < F < 100000` and `1 < C < 1000000`, else `400 { error }`. In one transaction: insert the job (`PENDING`) and its ⌈F/5⌉ GENERATE tasks (`fileIndexes` in chunks of 5, 0-based; use one `INSERT … SELECT generate_series(…)`). Commit, then call `refill()` (publishes up to `QUEUE_TARGET` tasks). Log event "job created". Return `202 { jobId }`. |
| `GET /jobs` | Newest 100 jobs: id, f, c, status, progress, created/started/finished, error. |
| `GET /jobs/:id` | Job fields + progress + task counts by status + files_generated. `404` if missing. |
| `GET /jobs/:id/result` | If `COMPLETED`: send `result.csv` as a download. Else `409 { status }`. |
| `DELETE /jobs/:id` | If `PENDING`/`RUNNING`: set `CANCELLED` + `finished_at`; set its `PENDING` tasks to `FAILED` (error "cancelled"). Else `409`. |
| `GET /workers` | All rows from `workers` (mark non-fresh as `DEAD` in the response). |
| `PUT /workers` | Body `{ count }`, integer 0–32, else `400`. Upsert `settings.desired_workers`. Return `{ desired }`. |
| `GET /stats` | `{ workers: {desired, idle, busy, draining, dead}, jobs: {waiting, running, completed, failed, cancelled}, tasks: {pending, queued, waitingInQueue, running, retries, backups} }`. `jobs.waiting` = `PENDING` jobs. |
| `GET /events?after=<id>` | Up to 100 events with `id > after`, oldest first. |
| `GET /` | Serves `public/index.html`. |

**Progress %** = `COMPLETED ? 100 : 100 × Σ(len(inputs) − 1 over DONE COMBINE tasks) / (F − 1)`.
SQL: `SUM(jsonb_array_length(payload->'inputs') - 1)`.

