## 10. Worker manager (`manager.py`)

```
seed settings: INSERT desired_workers = INITIAL_WORKERS ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
slowdowns = WORKER_SLOWDOWN split by comma
procs = {}               # index -> multiprocessing.Process
every 2 s:
    desired = settings.desired_workers
    remove exited processes from procs (restart any that crashed unexpectedly)
    alive = processes not asked to stop
    if len(alive) < desired: start new ones with the lowest free indexes,
                             slowdown = slowdowns[index % len(slowdowns)]
    if len(alive) > desired: send SIGTERM to the highest indexes (they drain, then exit)
on SIGTERM: terminate all children, wait, exit
```

