## 12. Edge cases (must work)

| Case | Expected behaviour |
|---|---|
| F = 2…5 | 1 GENERATE task, then one final COMBINE with F inputs |
| F = 6 | GENERATE 5 + 1; COMBINE 5 → partial; final COMBINE {partial, file 6} |
| F not a multiple of 5 | Last GENERATE task has fewer files; tree adapts |
| W = 0 | Jobs wait; resume when W > 0 |
| Worker killed mid-task | RabbitMQ redelivers; result still correct |
| Same result delivered twice | Second one ignored (`DONE` check, unique path) |
| Backup and original both finish | First accepted, second ignored |
| Cancel mid-job | No new tasks published; queued tasks come back as `SKIPPED`; late results ignored; queue counts stay correct |
| Task with > 5 inputs (bug) | Worker refuses it and reports `FAILED` |
| Two jobs at once | Both progress (round-robin) and both complete correctly |
| Scheduler restarted | Unacked results redelivered; tick re-plans; no loss |
| RabbitMQ restarted | Durable queues + persistent messages survive |
| Invalid input (`F = 1`, `C = 1000000`, `F = "abc"`) | `400` with a clear message |

